From ab89b2b057d0760503df7816971b16446f4c6e8e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 16:33:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] ws397: ES8311 mic capture through AudioManager (I2S full
 duplex, AudioConfig::din)

The ws397's mic is analog into the ES8311 (MIC1), so the PDM Microphone path
does not apply. Add the codec capture path to AudioManager:

- AudioConfig::din (defaulted, existing initializers unchanged): I2S data in
  from the codec's ASDOUT. ws397 = GPIO21 (vendor 01_Audio_Test).
  BoardConfig::hasCodecMic() reports it.
- ES8311 fed from the MCLK pin gets the vendor es8311_init() bring-up
  (reset 0x1F/0x00/0x80, reg01 0x3F, unity dividers, 16-bit I2S in/out,
  analog + ADC modulator + DAC powered, volume 0xB2). The BCLK-sourced M5
  sequence is untouched.
- The I2S port is created full duplex when the board has a codec mic: RX
  borrows TX's BCLK/WS, so playback and capture share one rate and TX stays
  enabled while capturing.
- beginCapture(rate) / readCapture(dst, n, timeout) / endCapture(): 16-bit
  mono from the left slot; codecCapture() powers the ADC/PGA and routes the
  analog mic per the vendor microphone_config (reg14 0x1A, reg17 0xC8).
- end(): full release (stop, power down, delete both channels) so a
  per-activity AudioManager can re-create the port later.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016HQ6nZag75VgtH5Z2WUGoF
